comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T22:52:07.806Z",codex-sol,"Comparison receipt: standalone pm-linked graph acceptance passed at 2513 ms; npm run release:check failed the 10000 ms read budget at 10959 ms; bun run release:check passed that same assertion at 8297 ms. Both full runs executed 493 tests with zero skips. Root cause is unproven; investigate suite instrumentation and read cost without changing thresholds. Existing fixture failures are separately tracked in pm-web-cqwm and pm-web-sspv."
  "2026-10-10T03:00:46.447Z",codex-sol,"SDK update candidate full unchanged coverage run fails large-corpus graph acceptance before reaching its 10000 ms assertion: the generatedAt parity assertion exceeds its 30000 ms tolerance. Whole test duration is 118193 ms, including fixture generation, so that is not a measured graph-read duration. Small generated graph parity and deterministic concurrent-create tests pass. Preserve both timing assertions; raw failed-run coverage is 90.04% statements/lines, 79.50% branches, 92.33% functions and no accepted coverage receipt remains."
  "2026-10-10T03:17:08.699Z",codex-sol,"Prior full run failed a 30-second cross-call timestamp tolerance before checking measured read latency. Standalone unchanged baseline reads 2000 real items in 6355 ms (2022 nodes, 23063 edges); total 21099 ms includes construction. Validate generatedAt against actual operation windows and check the unchanged 10000 ms read limit before payload parity. No production deadline or coverage inventory changes."
  "2026-10-10T03:23:17.622Z",codex-sol,"Focused combined acceptance exposes the unchanged read limit directly: 10918 ms, rejected (original standalone 6355 ms). Installed SDK source and declarations show listAllItemMetadataLight delegates to the same canonical candidate ordering as the full reader while skipping heavy collection hydration. Use light rows only for ID ordering; graph payloads still come exclusively from certified full rows, under the same workspace lock and external-writer guard. Real 2000-item full/light ordering equality and original payload/interleaving regressions are required. Serialize coverage test files to avoid suite fanout competing with its own latency measurement; retain every test, source and threshold."
  "2026-10-10T03:23:59.234Z",codex-sol,"Focused green after the public light ordering reader: 2/2 pass, zero skips; real queued/external writer guards pass, actual 2000-item read5586ms,2022nodes,23063relationships; full/light SDK ID ordering deep-equal. Prior combined full-reader run10918ms rejected by unchanged10000ms limit. Run complete serial coverage gate next; no capacity or deployment claim."
  "2026-10-10T04:08:06.156Z",codex-sol,"Verification receipt is recorded in docs/sdk-update-automation.md and linked from pm-web-8pml: complete release490/490,zero skips; packed npm/nativeBun4/4, six real disposablePostgreSQL collaboration tests. Keep item unclosed for independent orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-10T05:01:03.067Z",codex-sol,"PR #182 npm-link repair coverage rerun on unchanged graph source: 2000-item certified read measured 15811 ms, returning 2022 nodes and 23063 relationships, and correctly failed the retained 10000 ms assertion. Whole test duration 49518 ms includes fixture generation and is not read latency. Earlier base 4ff3ec receipt measured 3230 ms. No graph source, test deadline or threshold change; this known intermittent quality boundary prevents accepting the current coverage run. Catalog repair remains owned by pm-web-s99c; retain companion pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10 crosslinks."
  "2026-10-10T05:03:43.118Z",codex-sol,"Existing focused linked large-corpus check passes after packed installation completes: 1/1, zero skips, actual certified read 4495 ms, 2022 nodes and 23063 relationships; whole test 13267 ms includes generation. Same graph source and unchanged 10000 ms limit. Preserve the full instrumented-suite 15811 ms failure as a separate receipt; focused success does not accept that coverage run."
  "2026-10-10T05:13:11.676Z",codex-sol,"Final unchanged instrumented coverage retry passes 492/492 with zero skips after packed installation completes; actual 2000-item read 3257 ms (2022 nodes, 23063 relationships), within the original 10000 ms assertion. Keep prior full-suite 15811 ms failure and focused 4495 ms success as distinct receipts; no source, timing threshold or assertion edit. This bounded pass does not establish capacity or remove the intermittent-timing owner. Release claim, leave in progress for independent verification."
  "2026-10-11T06:41:15.786Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Reused existing latency investigation for the current dependency-update acceptance blocker (pm-web-8pml). Current SDK 2026.10.10 real 2000-item corpus yielded 12500 ms wall with full SDK scan 12084 ms wall / 2571 ms CPU and light ordering scan 207 ms wall / 33 ms CPU; second focused run yielded 27154 ms wall / 2728 ms CPU / 12488 involuntary context switches. Same 2022 nodes / 23063 edges, unchanged certified unbounded noExtensions read, queue and external-writer ID-set guard. Four CPUs are available under system load roughly 40 to 50. CPU cost remains consistent with the previously recorded 3230 ms full-gate success, while elapsed time inflates substantially. Added portable CPU/context-switch diagnostics to test/graph-export-fidelity.test.ts; preserving 10000 ms wall guard and coverage thresholds. Scheduler-wait measurement is in progress; no completed green current release gate yet."
  "2026-10-11T06:42:01.611Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Direct scheduler accounting confirms root cause is CPU scheduling contention: focused run 11104 ms wall / 2774 ms process CPU / 18059 involuntary context switches; main thread ran 2226 ms and spent 8161 ms runnable but unscheduled over 16808 time slices. Thus more than eight seconds of the fixed ten-second budget was scheduler wait, rather than SDK execution or tracker I/O. Temporary scheduler instrumentation restored; retained only portable wall/CPU/context-switch diagnostic. The production read, certified completeness and external-write refusal remain intact. A quieter acceptance window is required before further full gates; do not mark any failed or interrupted receipt green."
  "2026-10-11T07:02:07.187Z",codex-sol,"PR #175 round-1 correction validation reproduced the existing full-coverage graph latency failure. The 2000-item certified read measured 23045 ms; the unchanged large-corpus assertion failed. The four correction paths concern command arguments, failed-output display, selector rejection and SSE test cleanup, with no graph/runtime budget changes. Retain this as shared-host failure evidence alongside independent CI validation; do not relax the limit."
  "2026-10-11T07:17:11.802Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Linked own-author focused command pm test pm-web-hqqp --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 --json completed, with actual test result 0 passed / 1 failed / 0 skipped: 13674 ms wall, 2587 ms CPU, 15975 involuntary context switches for the same 2000-item/2022-node/23063-edge corpus. Failure category is assertion_failure, not sandbox PM_PATH, trust refusal or timeout; linked-test runner elapsed 60584 ms. The improved-load retry did not clear the unchanged 10000 ms guard, so full matrix remains blocked on scheduling. No source, cache or performance-threshold change accepted."
  "2026-10-11T07:29:57.730Z",codex-sol,"The complete Bun release command with isolated Git identity and explicit canonical fleet root also exceeds the unchanged 10000 ms large-corpus graph read limit: 12565 ms for 2000 items, 2022 nodes and 23063 edges. The twenty-seed export parity and concurrent/viewer regressions pass; the catalog consistency assertions pass with canonical discovery. This independently reproduces the timing boundary without changing graph source, source inventories or thresholds."
  "2026-10-11T07:34:24.666Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Draft checkpoint: latest linked focused graph command node --test --test-name-pattern=large-corpus test/graph-export-fidelity.test.ts failed 0 passed/1 failed/0 skipped at 13674 ms wall, 2587 ms CPU and 15975 involuntary context switches. Earlier scheduler accounting measured 8161 ms runnable wait versus 2226 ms main execution in an 11104 ms read; portable CPU/context diagnostics remain, temporary Linux instrumentation is removed. Complete linked npm gate failed 494/491/3/0 with graph 33136 ms plus collaboration and startup deadline failures; subsequent current npm gate interrupted after 18495 ms is incomplete. No Bun, actual-overlay full gates or isolated Git identity full gate is accepted yet. Preserve 10000 ms wall assertion, certified complete unbounded observational SDK read and unchanged coverage thresholds. Preparing one draft PR with explicit blocker while continuing local acceptance under the bounded eight-gate plan; claim stays active."
  "2026-10-11T07:35:14.276Z",codex-agent,"Orchestrator independently ran the unchanged large-corpus graph test directly against the disposable fixture on restored current SDK 2026.10.10: 1 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. 2000-item corpus produced 2022 nodes and 23063 edges; graph read 7962ms wall, 2617ms CPU, 11160 involuntary context switches, total test runner 44458.28ms. The 10000ms wall guard, complete certified noExtensions reader, source order and assertions were unchanged. This passing focused receipt justifies the next complete local replay; it does not certify the full release gate or prove scheduling will remain quiet."
  "2026-10-11T07:36:24.997Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Orchestrator independent current-SDK focused graph receipt passes 1/1 with unchanged 10000 ms wall limit: 7962 ms wall, 2617 ms CPU, 11160 involuntary context switches, same 2000 items / 2022 nodes / 23063 edges. This clears the focused prerequisite for one direct current npm run release:check replay now running, not acceptance of the full release. Draft https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/185 explicitly retains failed and pending gates."
  "2026-10-11T07:42:18.996Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Independent draft-head f0d8cad CI passes the unchanged graph guard within complete coverage suites: Node22 job 114418120287 read 1808 ms wall/2328 ms CPU/104 involuntary switches; Node26 job 114418120164 read 1434 ms wall/1671 ms CPU/60 switches. Both have 494 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. Local failed graph reads retain similar process CPU but much higher scheduling delay; root focused local receipt passes at 7962 ms wall/2617 ms CPU. Current direct local npm release replay continues; CI success does not replace requested local acceptance or eliminate the environmental wall-clock risk."
  "2026-10-11T07:52:49.199Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Direct current npm release replay completes at 494 total/493 passed/1 failed/0 skipped/0 cancelled, sole unchanged graph wall guard failure16606 ms with3400 ms CPU and12485 switches. Test duration847377.611353 ms; collaboration/startup pass, failed coverage S/L90.33%, B80.10%, F93.43% is discarded. Latest cacdb39 CI passes494/494 on Node22 and26, graph1288/1326 ms respectively (1600/1530 CPU). Existing local Node26.7.0/npm11.19.0 is available and matches the CI runtime major; focused real graph under V8 coverage running there to distinguish runtime cost from scheduling before the next complete gate. No production reader, caches, ordering scan or performance assertion changed."
  "2026-10-11T07:54:36.593Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Focused real graph under V8 coverage on existing Node26.7.0 passes 1/1/0skips at8178 ms wall/3006 ms CPU/16333 involuntary switches, runner28201.969295 ms. No partial diagnostic coverage is accepted as release evidence. One current npm run release:check replay begins on this existing CI-major runtime; full matrix waits for its result. The earlier complete Node24 replay remains493/494 with sole16606 ms graph failure."
  "2026-10-11T08:11:24.287Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Complete Node26 current npm gate passes graph6630 ms wall/2834 ms CPU but fails494 total/491 passed/3 failed/0 skips: three loopback ECONNRESET errors in CLI-backed HTTP contract fixtures. Failed S/L89.76%, B80.12%, F93.43% is discarded and unchanged thresholds still fail. This is a separate fixture blocker from graph scheduling: synchronous direct CLI verification prevents the shared HTTP event loop progressing. A deterministic real-tracker request-progress regression fails0/1 before helper repair, passes1/1 with asynchronous real CLI verification. Full contract regression running; graph reader and10000 ms guard unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T08:21:47.335Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Bounded next replay uses supported Node26. Last complete Node26 npm graph passed 6630 ms wall/2834 ms CPU/18811 involuntary switches, while the gate stayed red on three HTTP fixture fetch ECONNRESET cases (494/491/3/0). The fixture now awaits real CLI verification; linked full contracts pass 11/11 and helper-only revert fails 0/1. Graph guard remains 10000 ms wall with complete observational SDK reads and all assertions. Earlier complete graph failures and interrupted receipt remain recorded, not accepted; local complete eight-gate evidence is pending. Production and host scheduling settings remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-11T08:34:42.183Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"New-head local complete Node26 release fails only graph: 495/494/1/0/0, 10207mswall/2787msCPU/7794switches; all previously failing HTTP cases pass after real async CLI verifier fixture repair. Focused c8 graph also refuses10626mswall/3135msCPU/13991switches at0/1. Same-head independent CI graph passes1891ms Node22 and1478ms Node26, full495/495 each. Preserve10000ms wall guard and full observational SDK reads. No matrix progress or accepted local coverage; further retries bounded by observed scheduling conditions."
  "2026-10-11T08:37:03.991Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Improved scheduling evidence supports one bounded complete retry: portable CPU-only probe 500.002ms CPU/1110.755ms wall independently of SDK/filesystem work; then focused real graph under c8 passes1/1, zero skips, 3349ms wall/2660msCPU/18369 involuntary switches, complete2022nodes/23063edges with unchanged10000ms guard and ordering assertions. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node node_modules/c8/bin/c8.js --include src/**/*.ts --reporter=json-summary --reports-dir <scratch-coverage> node --test --test-name-pattern=large-corpus test/graph-export-fidelity.test.ts. Scratch coverage is diagnostic only. Next npm run release:check on restored SDK10.10; no failed receipt reclassified."
  "2026-10-11T08:51:56.142Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"FIRST GREEN complete local receipt on source head da1899652825c640de1dbd7ee2160972d16daffa: bun run release:check on current SDK2026.10.10 exits0, 495/495 tests,0 failed/skipped/cancelled; full command720.288s. Coverage all34 src files S/L90.33%, B80.11%, F93.43%, unchanged thresholds90/79/92. Graph7906mswall/2831msCPU/12632switches passes10000ms guard; complete graph/order assertions retained. Production audit zero vulnerabilities, packed real npm/Bun minimum/current hosts4/4, changelog/date/publish-attestation checks pass. Existing current npm remains failed495/494/1; no receipt rewritten. Remaining actual183npm,184npm,historical181npm/Bun,combined181183184Bun,cleanGitidentitynpm next; all other failures remain recorded separately."
  "2026-10-11T09:04:51.119Z",codex-sol-pm-web,"Second complete local green release: actual #183 workflow overlay npm495/495, zero skips, graph3595mswall/2491msCPU/17178switches. Current Bun also full495/495 withgraph7906ms. No runtime graph changes; existing current npm graph10207ms refusal remains failed evidence. Full observations/order/10sec guard unchanged; environment-sensitive risk remains open while independent overlays continue."
  "2026-10-11T10:04:02.436Z",codex-agent,"Verification complete for dependency-bump scope: all seven full local scenarios pass495/495, zero skips, unchanged graph wall guard and unchanged coverage thresholds. Graph diagnostics distinguish CPU from scheduling without changing acceptance. Async CLI-helper-only revert fails real HTTP-progress regression0/1; fixed route suite11/11. Existing scheduling issue remains open; keep original failed attempts as evidence. No production graph algorithm, timeout or hosted service change."
